# Update some fields of a Make scenario, and print it as JSON, with isinvalid and its flow
# Only the given fields change
# The Blueprint and the Scheduling are JSON, inline or from a file. The file wins
# A Blueprint that is sent is validated first: unique module IDs, a module and a version on every module, and the required fields of metadata.expect
# The command fails with the list of problems, and sends no request. It cannot detect an unsupported expression, such as a regex literal in replace
# Then the Blueprint is aligned: modules on one baseline, 300 apart, left to right. No option skips the validation or the alignment
# A Blueprint is saved with the version read just before, and the previous Blueprint is written to a backup file first. If someone saved the Scenario in between, Make answers 409, the command fails, and their edit stays
# When Make marks the new Blueprint as invalid, the previous Blueprint is sent back and the command exits non-zero with the messages of Make. If the restore fails, the error names the backup file
# Make rejects a Blueprint without a name (500), so give it one
# Usage:
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --name "Paris Meetup 2026"
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --blueprint '{"flow":[]}'
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --blueprint-file ./blueprint.json
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --scheduling '{"type":"on-demand"}'
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --scheduling-file ./scheduling.json
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --folderId 12
# $ make-scenario-update 925 --name "Paris" --account perso
setopt local_options err_return

local libDir="${functions_source[$0]:A:h:h}/__lib"
node "${libDir}/bin/make-scenario-update.js" "$@"
